       {
        "id": "p1",
        "description": "M1 writes $f(x + h) = 2(x + h)^{2} - 5(x + h) = 2x^{2} + 4xh + 2h^{2} - 5x - 5h$",
        "marks": 1
       },
       {
        "id": "p2",
        "description": "M1 simplifies $f(x + h) - f(x) = 4xh + 2h^{2} - 5h$",
        "marks": 1
       },
       {
        "id": "p3",
        "description": "M1 divides by $h$: $4x + 2h - 5$",
        "marks": 1
       },
       {
        "id": "p4",
        "description": "A1 lets $h \\to 0$ (limit stated) to obtain $f'(x) = 4x - 5$",
        "marks": 1
       }
      ]
     },
     "modelAnswer": "$$\nf(x + h) - f(x) = 2(x + h)^{2} - 5(x + h) - 2x^{2} + 5x = 4xh + 2h^{2} - 5h\n$$\n\n$$\nf'(x) = \\lim_{h \\to 0}\\frac{4xh + 2h^{2} - 5h}{h} = \\lim_{h \\to 0}(4x + 2h - 5) = 4x - 5\n$$"
    },
    "explanation": "Expand, subtract, cancel h, then take the limit."
   },
